From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <port@local>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 15:44:22 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] il2cpp: hook through libfusion and resolve export stubs

Three changes are needed before the chainloader can run on Android.

1. Native library name. The chainloader only ever tried to dlopen
   'GameAssembly', which is the Windows layout. Linux and Android ship
   libil2cpp.so.

2. Detour provider. Upstream detours through Dobby/Funchook loaded as
   separate libraries. Here the inline hook engine already lives inside
   libfusion.so, the library that hosts the CoreCLR bootstrap, so
   NativeDetour calls libfusion's hook/unhook exports and Il2CppInterop is
   pointed at NativeDetourProvider. CacheDetourWrapper keeps the delegate and
   the generated trampoline reachable, because CoreCLR collects them otherwise.
   The Desktop-only detour types are removed rather than left behind unused.

3. Export stub resolution. il2cpp_runtime_invoke is reached through a linker
   stub, not the function body: on ELF it is a single B instruction, sometimes
   behind a literal-pool veneer. Dobby cannot patch a 4-byte stub, and doing so
   produces a broken prologue or a SIGILL under pointer authentication.
   ExportThunkResolver follows those stubs explicitly, bounded and with a hop
   limit, then validates the result against /proc/self/maps so a detached or
   unresolvable address fails loudly instead of being hooked.
